Z||000006||Cozmo||07-30-2001||01:21 PM||||I agree, a change of pace from red is nice...<BR>Terry, that engine looks great!<BR>I decided on gold for my Targa, since the car will be green eventually.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-031f.jpg"> <BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||14
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||07-30-2001||01:29 PM||||I'm assuming these were all repainted off the engine... it it necessary (as it appears)to remove the lower plenum to get the valve covers off, or is there a nifty trick to getting them off without having to disassemble the entire top end of the engine?<P>Mine need repainting, but it has waited this long because it looks like a *huge* job just to get the rear valve cover off...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rob Durham||07-30-2001||01:30 PM||||You guy's have done some awesome work on detailing your engine bays<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">  </A>||||reg||6
Z||000009||87ECO5||07-30-2001||02:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>is it necessary (as it appears)to remove the lower plenum to get the valve covers off, or is there a nifty trick to getting them off without having to disassemble the entire top end of the engine?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I removed the "intermediate" intake manifold in order to remove/install the rocker arm covers but I've heard it can be done with the intake components in place.<P>I did it because I didn't want to scratch the freshly-painted rocker arm covers during reassembly.||||reg||1
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||07-30-2001||03:06 PM||||What type of paint are you guys using to color the engine?  I have a Green car as well and have thought about the gold intake/valve covers. Although the red is a good contrast-<P>-Thanks<BR>Rob<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cozmo||07-30-2001||03:19 PM||||I used Rust-oleum Hammered finish spray bombs. It goes on really good and seems very tough.  The "beaded" finish hides surface imperfections and it comes in a bunch of colors.<BR>I was lucky <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> since I had mine all apart to do the head gaskets, so it was easy to paint.  Don't know about tearing all that stuff off just to paint the plenum and valve covers, seems like a lot of work... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
Z||000012||b lo 0||07-30-2001||03:24 PM||||A-tgowens, SWEET motor.  Did the 2.8 stuff bolt right on?<P>B-Lzeitgeist-I have the same problem.  Looks a little cramped in there, huh?<P>C-MinnGreenGT-I always use VHT Hi-Temp coatings.  Best quality, IMHO.  Get it a Pep Boys or in Summit<P>D-I plan on putting several coats of white on mine and buffing it out to get rid of the texture and get a smooth, high gloss finish.  Then the exposed aluminum fins are getting polished.  I already polished the throttle body-looks sweet.  I dunno.  Should I go white (matches car), or red and coordinate hoses, loom, brake calipers, ETC?  I need opinions...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||07-30-2001||08:47 PM||||Hi Terry, I saw that motor setup in the shop with the big 8.5mm BLUE wires, all I can say is *georgous!*<P>I meant to ask, are those just the stock manifolds ceramic coated? They look great!<P>I can't wait to see (and feel the 3.4 :) in the car!<P><BR>PS: Body Coloured phlenums rule, I think you and George may have started a trend!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||LT1 Chop Top||07-30-2001||08:53 PM||||Tgowens,<P>Very nice set up!  Where did you get the work done, and how much $??  I really like the headers!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Neal||07-30-2001||09:38 PM||||I wish i had a digital camera, and id take pictures.  I JUST finished painting my intake and valve covers a wrinkle black and the engraved FIERO is a cherry red, the block and heads will be the same cherry red, and the oil pan will be painted silver.<P>i would like to see plenum and valve covers gun metal grey with a black block and silver whereever else possible.||||reg||1
Z||000016||tgowens||07-31-2001||12:15 AM||||ok, let me see if I can answer some of you...<P><B>Monkeyman</B>, the color is High Heat Aluminum. It is a Dupli-Color Ceramic 1200 degree paint...<P><B>Cozmo</B>, thanks, I appreciate the compliment.<P><B>LZeitgeist</B>, yes, all of the pieces were painted prior to assembling the engine. The trick to removing the valve covers is removing the brackets (front and rear) that interfere with the removal of the valve cover bolts. Also, it helps if the decklid is off!<P><B>MinnGreenGT</B>, I use high heat ceramic paint for the block and manifolds and the plenum and valve covers were stripped, primed, sprayed with a metalflake paint, then polished and then clear coated...I'll have to take a picture of George's (George Miller of Fiero Shop), he has a green '88 GT with green plenum and valve covers...<P><B>b lo 0</B>, thank you. Yes, everything from the heads up from the 2.8 bolts on to the 3.4.<P><B>Ben</B>, thank you. Those are the stock manifolds sprayed with a ceramic paint but I have a set of headers coming that I will install prior to putting the engine on the cradle. I'll let ya know when I get it completed and you are more than welcome to drop by and drive it..<P><B>LT1 Chop Top</B>, Thanks, I do all the work myself so the only cost is for the materials. The paint runs $4.99 a can...<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000017||fiero56||07-31-2001||11:30 PM||||Terry, that is one bad(in a good way) looking engine. That timing cover is going to be blinding in the sun with the decklid up.<P>Will that paint on those manifolds hold up to the heat, or would it burn off?<P>Are you using Dupli-color exclusively on thast engine, or other brands too? I'm curious to what colors other than primary colors are available in high-heat.<P>Still no pics of a shiny grey 2.8, I like how that sounds. I bet when I finish, all 1200 members with grey 2.8s will post pictures along with mine <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I've seen the factory grey on other chevy 2.8s, ugly. I'm thinking darker, and more reflective. Think of the body color of the 'stang on Gone In Sixty Seconds, something similar to that.<P>You have mail Terry <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR>||||reg||1
